<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1568) <span class="when">Oct 14, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Frame by frame through a conformed cut.</b> The arrow keys go on from a clip's last frame into the next event, and back from its first into the one before, as an edit application does. A layer stacked over a shot (V2 and up) is no longer the next clip shown when stepping, playing on or going to the next clip; click it in the Conform window to see it.</li>
<li><b>Footage Offline.</b> A conformed clip whose footage isn't there shows a Footage Offline card with its name and Record TC, for as long as the cut holds it, instead of the clip before it.</li>
<li><b>RETIME ≈.</b> A quiet pill beside the clip's name says when its retime plays only approximately: a ramp, played at its average speed.</li>
<li><b>Where each plate came from.</b> Pull Plates writes plates/main/source_info.txt in either folder layout, as vfx edit commit does, and each line and the shot's conform text now also give the clip as the cut names it (its scene and take) and the Source TC the cut uses.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 1476) <span class="when">Oct 12, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>DPX sequences play.</b> 8, 10, 12 and 16-bit DPX files open and play like any other image sequence, read as the color space set for DPX in Settings, Color.</li>
<li>A tall floating Playlist with thumbnails could stop the app. Fixed.</li>
<li>Small fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1441) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Network is in the Review menu.</b> Review ▸ Network; it was under Window. It is also in the right-click Review menu.</li>
<li><b>A playlist on a network drive no longer slows the window.</b> Whether each clip's file is there is checked in the background.</li>
<li><b>Locate Media… reads a folder in the background.</b> A line above the toolbar says how far it has got.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1430) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Small fixes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1427) <span class="when">Oct 11, 2026</span></h3>
