</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 1565) <span class="when">Oct 14, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>The Edit Ref on screen follows the cut.</b> In 1.0 (1557) and (1561) the Edit Ref drawn beside the conform was the conform's own frame number plus the Line up offset, so going from shot to shot showed parts of it out of order (frame grabs and the Record TC were right). It is now drawn at the frame of the cut the conform is showing, and runs on through a freeze.</li>
<li><b>Line Up by Picture.</b> An Edit Ref with black or a slate before the cut, and no timecode to say so, no longer has to be lined up by eye: Line Up by Picture finds the offset from where its cuts fall against the cut's, checks a frame of up to ten shots, and offers it (Apply +7). Nothing moves until you apply it.</li>
<li><b>Trim Handles on a conformed clip.</b> A clip of a conformed cut plays only the frames the cut uses. Trim Handles used to widen it to the whole camera file, and the Edit Ref beside it stopped following; it now leaves the clip alone, and a session saved that way plays the clip's own frames again.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
